<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	Deliberately empty.

	The hardened runtime is required for notarization, and every entitlement added here is a
	hole punched back through it. Ultra spawns login shells and PTYs, and that needs NO
	entitlement: a child process is its own process with its own signature, not code loaded
	into ours.

	What might genuinely be needed later, and only once something is observed to fail:

	  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
	      if a plug-in or an injected library has to load into Ultra itself.
	  com.apple.security.cs.allow-dyld-environment-variables
	      if DYLD_* set in a shell has to reach a process Ultra spawned.

	Neither is added on a guess. An entitlement granted speculatively is indistinguishable
	from one that was needed, so the next person cannot tell which are load-bearing.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
